# Simple AIOps pipeline — project document (single file)

**Scope:** The educational demo under `simple_aiops_pipeline/`: what AIOps means here, data flow, detection internals, metrics, artifacts, Git, bundle export, and how it relates to real AIOps stacks.

**Code root:** `simple_aiops_pipeline/` (full path depends on your clone).

**Git:** `simple_aiops_pipeline/GIT_EDUCATION.md`.

---

## 1. What AIOps means (in one paragraph)

**AIOps** usually means applying analytics and ML to **IT operations data** (metrics, logs, traces, alerts) to **detect anomalies**, **reduce noise**, **correlate** incidents, or **prioritize** work. This repo is a **toy**: synthetic KPIs, a **rolling z-score** baseline (classic ops + stats), and **precision/recall** against injected ground truth so you can teach evaluation without plugging into Prometheus on day one.

